IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 268 (piece dg8, lines 1382 to 1385):
-- amendments to the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation; disclosure schedules.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation that is a party to a merger: a director asked to approve a merger agreement
-- that is silent on the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, a stockholder asked to approve an agreement whose disclosure schedules are not attached.
-- The seat layer dg8-seat.l4 asks these rules from that side.
--
-- Section 268 is not among the sections section 114(b) and (c) take out of the reading of "stockholder" as "member" and "board of directors" as "governing body" for a nonstock corporation.
-- Section 251(g) (piece dg6) is the one merger the subsection leaves out; it is taken as an input.

§ `s 268(a) The agreement of merger and the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation`

-- The subsection applies to a constituent corporation where an agreement of merger entered into under any provision of the subchapter other than section 251(g) provides, for that corporation, that all of its issued and
-- outstanding shares of capital stock immediately before the merger becomes effective shall be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities (excluding stock of the surviving corporation).
-- src:1383 | (a) If an agreement of merger entered into pursuant to any provision of this subchapter, other than § 251(g) of this title, provides, with respect to any constituent corporation, that all of the shares of capital stock of such constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the time at which the merger becomes effective shall be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities (excluding stock of the surviving corporation), …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a) (src:1383)
GIVEN `the agreement of merger was entered into pursuant to § 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 251(g) (piece dg6)
      `the agreement provides that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 268(a) the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` MEANS
        (NOT `the agreement of merger was entered into pursuant to § 251(g)`)
    AND `the agreement provides that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation`

-- (i): "the agreement of merger as approved by the board of directors need not include any provision regarding the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in order for the agreement
-- of merger to be considered in final form or substantially final form". The director's side: the board may approve an agreement that is silent on it.
-- src:1383 | then, notwithstanding any other provision of this subchapter, with respect to such constituent corporation, (i) the agreement of merger as approved by the board of directors need not include any provision regarding the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in order for the agreement of merger to be considered in final form or substantially final form, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(i) (src:1383)
GIVEN `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(a)(i) the agreement approved by the board need not include any provision regarding the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` MEANS
    IF `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 268(a)(ii) Who may adopt an amendment of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` IS ONE OF
    `the board of directors of the constituent corporation`
    `a person acting at the direction of the board of directors of the constituent corporation`
    `the board of directors or governing body of a constituent entity whose shares or equity interests are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation`
    `a person acting at the direction of the board of directors or governing body of such a constituent entity`
    `any other person`

-- (ii): "any amendment or amendment and restatement of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation may be adopted by the board of directors of such constituent corporation or any person acting at the
-- direction thereof (or, if under the terms of the agreement of merger the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation,
-- the board of directors or governing body of such constituent entity or other person acting at the direction thereof)". A person the subsection does not name is not covered by it (NOTHING): other provisions
-- of the subchapter may still let that person adopt an amendment.
-- src:1383 | (ii) any amendment or amendment and restatement of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation may be adopted by the board of directors of such constituent corporation or any person acting at the direction thereof (or, if under the terms of the agreement of merger the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation, the board of directors or governing body of such constituent entity or other person acting at the direction thereof), …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(ii) (src:1383)
GIVEN who IS A `s 268(a)(ii) Who may adopt an amendment of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation`
      `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the terms of the agreement of merger the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(a)(ii) the person may adopt an amendment of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `any other person` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the board of directors of the constituent corporation` THEN JUST `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation`
    WHEN `a person acting at the direction of the board of directors of the constituent corporation` THEN JUST `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation`
    WHEN `the board of directors or governing body of a constituent entity whose shares or equity interests are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation`
         THEN JUST (`the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` AND `under the terms of the agreement of merger the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation`)
    WHEN `a person acting at the direction of the board of directors or governing body of such a constituent entity`
         THEN JUST (`the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` AND `under the terms of the agreement of merger the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation`)

-- (iii): "no alteration or change of such certificate of incorporation shall be deemed to constitute an amendment to the agreement of merger". Where the subsection applies the answer to "is it deemed an amendment?"
-- is no; where it does not apply the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1383 | and (iii) no alteration or change of such certificate of incorporation shall be deemed to constitute an amendment to the agreement of merger.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(iii) (src:1383)
GIVEN `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(a)(iii) the alteration or change of the certificate of incorporation is deemed an amendment to the agreement of merger` MEANS
    IF `the subsection applies to the constituent corporation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 268(b) Disclosure schedules`

-- "Unless otherwise expressly provided by an agreement of merger or consolidation, any disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or similar documents or instruments delivered in connection with the agreement that modify,
-- supplement, qualify, or make exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement shall not be deemed part of the agreement for purposes of any provision of this title
-- but shall have the effects provided in the agreement." Where the agreement expressly provides otherwise, or the document is not of that kind, the subsection does not decide whether it is part of the agreement (NOTHING).
-- src:1384 | (b) Unless otherwise expressly provided by an agreement of merger or consolidation, any disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or similar documents or instruments delivered in connection with the agreement that modify, supplement, qualify, or make exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement shall not be deemed part of the agreement for purposes of any provision of this title but shall have the effects provided in the agreement.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(b) (src:1384)
GIVEN `the document is a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or a similar document or instrument delivered in connection with the agreement that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(b) the disclosure schedule is part of the agreement for purposes of any provision of the title` MEANS
    IF   `the document is a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or a similar document or instrument delivered in connection with the agreement that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement`
     AND (NOT `the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provides otherwise`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1384 | but shall have the effects provided in the agreement.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(b) (src:1384)
GIVEN `the document is a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or a similar document or instrument delivered in connection with the agreement that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 268(b) the disclosure schedule has the effects provided in the agreement` MEANS
        `the document is a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or a similar document or instrument delivered in connection with the agreement that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions contained in the agreement`
    AND (NOT `the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provides otherwise`)
